136:   | L4 | Fine print (consent, legal) | `.tm-text-body-sm` 12/16, `--tm-content-secondary` |
161:   **Component anatomy keeps its own listed values** (they are part of the component, not screen spacing): OTP boxes 8 apart (L1), chip grid 8 / 8, wheel column heads 4, value label → value 4, sheet content → actions 24, the pinned bar's notice → button 16 and caption → button 8.
223:| OTP code | 56 boxes 8 apart (L1). Boxes (+ the reserved message line) → **32** → "Didn't receive it? Resend" → **32** → legal line → **8** → Verify. Locked / expired-and-limited: boxes → **16** → notice → **32** → Verify. | D-44, D-108 |
226:| Pinned bar | Padding 16 + safe area. Buttons 56/18, primary → quiet, 8 apart (box). Bar notice: full-width band, centred, 16 above its button. Caption line ("Available until 7:45 PM"): L3 centred, 8 above its button. The content scrolls, with ≥ 16 clear at the end. | `.tm-actionbar`, §9.5 |
250:| L6 | Logo → title: **16** (`--tm-space-lg`) on every screen with the logo (sign-in, OTP, faster sign-in offer, returning unlock, Home). D-107, 2026-11-11; was "sign-in 48, home-base hero gap" (D-46). |
308:| **Notice** | Neutral / warning / error (L5); stays until the cause is gone. **Warning** when something blocks the main action or runs on a timer (offline, locks, near expiry); **error** when an action failed; **neutral** only for side information (D-54). Text wraps balanced (A-22). **Placement (A-19, Round 4 item 2, 2026-11-02):** a notice that is the **result of an action** sits next to the control that did it — on a screen with a pinned bar, inside the bar above its button, in the band style of §3 (Home "ending soon", setup / add / request failures, the offer's "Couldn't turn on…", the case and calling bar notices); on a screen without a bar, 16 below the field it came from (D-98) or 8 below the button (A-14). A notice about **the bar's own action** — the result of the last tap, or why its button is disabled now (offline, "No cases right now") — is also in the bar. A notice about the **screen's general situation** (unlock "isn't available", Home idle-expired, manually ended, expired-pending, stop-pending) stays at the top of the panel, not tied to a button (lane-request 7, Round 4). **Alignment (D-86, 2026-11-03):** the band inside the bar is centred (icon and text as a group, wrapped lines centred, balanced breaks kept); every other notice (top of page, inside sheets, in content) stays left-aligned. |
