  1050	### D-108 · Spacing is measured on what the eye sees; one screen standard below the band — 2026-11-11
  1051	- **Decision (Apurva):** gaps are measured between **visible** edges (text, shapes, borders), never between layout boxes. Tap areas and reserved message lines may not add visible space.
  1052	  - **8** joins parts of one thing: label ↔ field, field ↔ its helper, a legal line ↔ the button it describes, a picture tile ↔ its caption.
  1053	  - **16** separates items inside one group (chips, points, cards stacked, rows).
  1054	  - **32** separates different things: a field group, an error or notice box, a link line, a button, a hero tile and the content under it.
  1055	  - Notices: a message about one field sits 16 under that field and 32 above the next thing; a message about the whole screen (locked, unavailable) sits at the top of its content or under the thing it blocks, then 32 to the next thing. A notice inside the pinned bar keeps the bar's own spec (16 above its button).
  1056	  - Applied: sign-in field + helper → 32 → Send OTP; sign-in "Couldn't send the OTP." 16 under the field, 32 above Send OTP; OTP code boxes (+ message line) → 32 → "Didn't receive it? Resend" → 32 → legal line → 8 → Verify; OTP locked / expired-limited: boxes → 16 → notice → 32 → Verify; offer hero → 32 → points (16 apart); unlock tile → 16 → caption.
  1057	  - The rest of the screen standard is `docs/renders/2026-11-11-screens-audit/CONCLUSION.md` §1, with these visible-gap values replacing its box values where they differ (e.g. its OTP legal → Verify 16 becomes 8 visible; notice → button 8 becomes 32).
  1058	  - **An automatic check measures visible gaps on every screen and state**; a failing check stops the build.
  1059	- **Why:** both audits passed screens that looked cramped (sign-in) next to screens that looked airy (OTP) because they counted boxes: OTP's visible gaps were 59 / 47 while its box gaps were 8 / 16. Rules written screen by screen ("a notice sits 8 above its button") had no shared principle.
  1060	
  1061	### D-109 · Copy batch, sheet subtitle, unlock prompt on arrival — 2026-11-11
  1062	- **Decision (Apurva, main thread's picks):**
  1063	  1. **Copy:** sign-in helper "We'll send you an OTP by SMS." · sign-in error "Couldn't send the OTP." · add-time sheet title "Add time" · end sheet "You won't get new cases…" · offer point 1 "Sign in with one touch" / "No SMS to wait for." (Face ID "with a glance", screen lock "with your PIN or pattern") · "New code sent." Vocabulary: **OTP** outside the OTP screen, **code** on it; **faster sign-in**; **availability** (window), **time** (length), **case**, **get** (new cases).
  1064	  2. **Sheets:** the subtitle sits 8 under the title inside the sheet header (design-system component).
  1065	  3. **Returning unlock:** the phone's fingerprint / Face ID / screen-lock prompt opens by itself once when the app opens; cancelling shows today's screen; the Unlock button stays for a retry. Amends D-38 / D-105.
  1066	- **Why:** consistent words across the entry screens; a floating sheet subtitle read as content; industry practice (prompt on arrival) saves a tap every open.
  1067	
